{"halonantaraH sanyogaH": [{"id": "halo'nantarAH saMyogaH", "headword": "हलोऽनन्तराः संयोगः", "headword_slp1": "halo'nantarAH saMyogaH", "fold": "halonantaraH sanyogaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "Consonants unseparated by a vowel are called conjunct consonants.\n\nTerms:", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["हलोऽनन्तराः संयोगः १.१.७", "१.१.७", "१.१.७ हलोऽनन्तराः संयोगः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["halo'nantarAH saMyogaH १.१.७", "१.१.७", "१.१.७ halo'nantarAH saMyogaH"]}], "halantaca": [{"id": "halantAcca", "headword": "हलन्ताच्च", "headword_slp1": "halantAcca", "fold": "halantaca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "And after a root ending in a consonant and preceded by a vowel of the प्रत्यहार इक् , the affix सन् beginning witha झल् consonant, is like कित् ।\n\nTerms: कित्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["हलन्ताच्च १.२.१०", "१.२.१०", "१.२.१० हलन्ताच्च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["halantAcca १.२.१०", "१.२.१०", "१.२.१० halantAcca"]}], "halantyam": [{"id": "halantyam", "headword": "हलन्त्यम्", "headword_slp1": "halantyam", "fold": "halantyam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In उपदेश , the final consonant of roots etc. is इत्।\n\nTerms: इत्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["हलन्त्यम् १.३.३", "१.३.३", "१.३.३ हलन्त्यम्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["halantyam १.३.३", "१.३.३", "१.३.३ halantyam"]}], "halaH snaH sanajJO": [{"id": "halaH SnaH SAnajJO", "headword": "हलः श्नः शानज्झौ", "headword_slp1": "halaH SnaH SAnajJO", "fold": "halaH snaH sanajJO", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix शानच् is the substitute of श्ना after a root ending with a consonant, when हि follows.\n\nTerms: शानच्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["हलः श्नः शानज्झौ ३.१.८३", "३.१.८३", "३.१.८३ हलः श्नः शानज्झौ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["halaH SnaH SAnajJO ३.१.८३", "३.१.८३", "३.१.८३ halaH SnaH SAnajJO"]}], "halasukarayoH puvaH": [{"id": "halasUkarayoH puvaH", "headword": "हलसूकरयोः पुवः", "headword_slp1": "halasUkarayoH puvaH", "fold": "halasukarayoH puvaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix ष्ट्रन् is used after the verb पू 'to purify' with the sense of instrument when denoting a member of the body of a plough or of a hog.\n\nTerms: ष्ट्रन्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["हलसूकरयोः पुवः ३.२.१८३", "३.२.१८३", "३.२.१८३ हलसूकरयोः पुवः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["halasUkarayoH puvaH ३.२.१८३", "३.२.१८३", "३.२.१८३ halasUkarayoH puvaH"]}], "halasca": [{"id": "halaSca", "headword": "हलश्च", "headword_slp1": "halaSca", "fold": "halasca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "And after a verb ending in a consonant, comes the affix घञ् (when the word to be formed is masculine and related to the verb as an instrument or a location and thereby the palatal is changed into guttural).\n\nTerms: घञ्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["हलश्च ३.३.१२१", "३.३.१२१", "३.३.१२१ हलश्च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["halaSca ३.३.१२१", "३.३.१२१", "३.३.१२१ halaSca"]}], "halasirawWak": [{"id": "halasIrAwWak", "headword": "हलसीराट्ठक्", "headword_slp1": "halasIrAwWak", "fold": "halasirawWak", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'this is his' after the words 1. हल and 2. सीर।\n\nTerms: ठक्", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'what bears it' after the words 1. हल and 2. सीर in Accusative -2nd case construction.\n\nTerms: ठक्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["हलसीराट्ठक् ४.३.१२४", "हलसीराट्ठक् ४.४.८१", "४.३.१२४", "४.३.१२४ हलसीराट्ठक्", "४.४.८१", "४.४.८१ हलसीराट्ठक्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["halasIrAwWak ४.३.१२४", "halasIrAwWak ४.४.८१", "४.३.१२४", "४.३.१२४ halasIrAwWak", "४.४.८१", "४.४.८१ halasIrAwWak"]}], "halNyabByo dirGat‌ sutisyapfktan hal": [{"id": "halNyAbByo dIrGAt‌ sutisyapfktaM hal", "headword": "हल्ङ्याब्भ्यो दीर्घात्‌ सुतिस्यपृक्तं हल्", "headword_slp1": "halNyAbByo dIrGAt‌ sutisyapfktaM hal", "fold": "halNyabByo dirGat‌ sutisyapfktan hal", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After a consonant there is the elision of the nominative affix स् and the tense-affix ति and सि (when reduced to the form of त् and स् ) being consonants; and so also after the long vowels ई and आ of the feminine (affix ङी and आप् ), there is the elision of the nominative affix स्।\n\nTerms:", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["हल्ङ्याब्भ्यो दीर्घात्‌ सुतिस्यपृक्तं हल् ६.१.६८", "६.१.६८", "६.१.६८ हल्ङ्याब्भ्यो दीर्घात्‌ सुतिस्यपृक्तं हल्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["halNyAbByo dIrGAt‌ sutisyapfktaM hal ६.१.६८", "६.१.६८", "६.१.६८ halNyAbByo dIrGAt‌ sutisyapfktaM hal"]}], "haladantat‌ saptamyaH sanjYayam": [{"id": "haladantAt‌ saptamyAH saMjYAyAm", "headword": "हलदन्तात्‌ सप्तम्याः संज्ञायाम्", "headword_slp1": "haladantAt‌ saptamyAH saMjYAyAm", "fold": "haladantat‌ saptamyaH sanjYayam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The Locative -7th case ending is not elided after a stem ending in a consonant or a short अ when the compound is a Name.\n\nTerms: विभक्ति-Non-elision", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["हलदन्तात्‌ सप्तम्याः संज्ञायाम् ६.३.९", "६.३.९", "६.३.९ हलदन्तात्‌ सप्तम्याः संज्ञायाम्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["haladantAt‌ saptamyAH saMjYAyAm ६.३.९", "६.३.९", "६.३.९ haladantAt‌ saptamyAH saMjYAyAm"]}], "halaH": [{"id": "halaH", "headword": "हलः", "headword_slp1": "halaH", "fold": "halaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The long vowel is substituted for a vocalised half-vowel अ , इ and उ at the end of a अङ्ग (stem), when it is preceded by a consonant which is a portion of the stem.\n\nTerms: Lengthening", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["हलः ६.४.२", "६.४.२", "६.४.२ हलः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["halaH ६.४.